---
title: Mock Chicken
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Meat, Poultry, Fish
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@veal{1%lb}
@pork{1%lb}
@salted water
@slices of bread{3}
@well-beaten eggs{3}

Cut @veal{1%lb} and @pork{1%lb} into cubes. Cover with salted water and cook until tender. Put @slices of bread{3} in the broth. Add @well-beaten eggs{3} to the mixture and stir. Put in a shallow baking dish. Bake for 1 hour at 350 degrees.
